<title>USA: Laboratory Corp says settles with U.S. Govt.</title>
<headline>Laboratory Corp says settles with U.S. Govt.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, N.C. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laboratory Corp said on Thursday it had agreed to pay the U.S. government $187 million to settle federal investigations into allegedly fraudulent billing practices.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the agreement, the company said it agreed to pay $182 million to settle civil claims involving Medicare and related government billings undertaken by its predecessor companies, National Health Laboratories Inc, Roche Biomedical Laboratories Inc, and Allied Clinical Laboratories Inc.</p>
</text>
